Subject: moldat.f and the seven files sharing COMMON /MOLMEC/: bound NHCO

WHAT IT FIXES
  MOPAC 7 finds the peptide torsions it will correct by walking the geometry
  for `O=C-N-H` and filling

      COMMON /MOLMEC/ HTYPE(4),NHCO(4,20),NNHCO,ITYPE

  two entries at a time, with no bound check anywhere in the loop:

                     NNHCO=NNHCO+1
                     NHCO(1,NNHCO)=I

  Twenty entries is ten amide N-H bonds. The twenty-first write lands on the
  word directly after the array, which is NNHCO itself, and the ones after
  that leave the COMMON block. Nothing reports it, and the run continues.

  Measured on this build, AM1, clusters of formamide (two amide N-H each, so
  four entries each) at 12 A separation, and controls that hold the system
  size fixed while changing only the number of entries:

      5 formamide + 1 benzene      20 entries  42 atoms   -193.60094 kcal/mol
      5 formamide + 2 benzene      20 entries  54 atoms   -171.15896 kcal/mol
      5 formamide + 1 NMA          22 entries  42 atoms  NOMM +4282.88497
      6 formamide                  24 entries  36 atoms  NOMM +5926.74987

  Under NOMM the heat of formation comes back positive by four thousand
  kcal/mol with no warning of any kind; under MMOK the SCF does not converge
  and MOPAC stops. The break is exactly at twenty entries and does not move
  with the atom count, so it is the array bound and not the chemistry.

  It is reachable by any peptide with more than ten unmethylated amide
  linkages -- a twelve-residue polyglycine is 48 heavy atoms and 38
  hydrogens, well inside this build.

WHAT IT DOES
  Raises NHCO to 120 entries, which is sixty amide N-H bonds and therefore
  more than any molecule this build can hold (each needs its own hydrogen,
  and MAXLIT is 56), in all eight files that declare COMMON /MOLMEC/ -- the
  block must stay one layout, which is what patch 0007 is about. The array is
  INTEGER and uninitialised, so it costs 1,600 bytes of .bss and nothing in
  the binary.

  Adds the bound check the loop never had, so that a SIZES raised past this
  one halts with its reason printed instead of writing over NNHCO. The label
  is 175, which was free, and the GOTO 225 around it keeps the normal path at
  one unconditional branch.

